.TH JEVTRI 1 "2026-09-30" "jevtri 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jevtri \- rank server logs by which to examine first after an incident
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jevtri
.RB [ \-t
.IR TIME ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR TEXT ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B jevtri init
.br
.B jevtri report
.br
.B jevtri
.RB [ \-\-help " [" \-\-lang
.IR LANG ]]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jevtri
collects the lines around an incident time from the configured logs, masks
secrets in them, and asks the Jev API how worth investigating each log is.
It prints the logs in order of
.IR "investigation priority" ,
from 0 to 100.
.PP
The priority is not the probability that a log holds the cause.
.B jevtri
recommends where to start reading; it does not find the cause, repair
anything, or watch the server.
Some failures leave no trace in any log.
When every log scores low,
.B jevtri
says so and suggests looking at logs that are not configured, at the
application, or outside the host.
.PP
Run
.B jevtri
as root so that it can read the logs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " \fITIME\fR"
Incident time, as
.I HH:MM[:SS]
(today, or yesterday if that is in the future) or
.IR "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM[:SS]" .
The default is now.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minutes " \fIN\fR"
Minutes to look at: before and after the time given with
.BR \-t ,
or the last
.I N
minutes without it.
The default is
.B minutes
in the configuration, 5.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-issue " \fITEXT\fR"
The symptom, in any language, for example
.IR "\(dqThe website returns 502\(dq" .
It is sent to Jev with the logs.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Configuration file. The default is
.IR /etc/jevtri/jevtri.conf .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also show the window, the lines and bytes read and sent per log, the number of
masked values, and Jev's raw answer. Log contents are not shown.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print JSON. Its
.B priority
is between 0 and 1.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show exactly what would be sent, and send nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " LANG"
Language of
.BR \-\-help :
.BR en ,
.B ja
or
.BR zh\-CN .
Without it, the language follows
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
or
.BR LANG .
Results and error messages are always in English.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH INIT
.B jevtri init
lists the known logs that exist on this server, lets you choose them by
number (such as
.B "1 3\-4" ;
empty for all), and checks the time format of each against its last lines.
Other paths can be added.
For a log whose time format is not known, it shows the first 10 lines (masked)
and asks before sending them to Jev to identify the format.
The answer is only registered if the lines really read that way.
.PP
If the configuration exists,
.B init
only adds
.B time_format
to logs that lack it, and changes nothing else.
Running
.B jevtri
without a configuration starts
.B init
in a terminal, and fails otherwise (cron, systemd timers, pipes).
.PP
.B jevtri report
helps improve jevtri with real incidents.
It lists the runs in the send log that Jev answered, asks which log really
showed the cause and for a one-line note, and writes a Markdown report to
.I case\-YYYYMMDD\-HHMMSS.md
next to the send log (mode 0600).
The host name, the user names of people (UID 1000 and above) and IP
addresses are replaced with labels such as
.BR [host\-1] ,
.B [user\-1]
and
.BR [ip\-1] .
Nothing is sent: the report is for the public issue form of the jevtri
repository, whose address is printed.
The issue is public, so read the report and remove other host names, system account names and
anything else before posting it.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is an INI file:
.B [general]
and one
.BI "[log " NAME ]
section per log, with
.I key
=
.I value
lines. Lines starting with
.B #
are comments. Errors are reported with the line number.
.PP
.B [general]
.TP
.B minutes
Default for
.BR \-m .
.TP
.B max_bytes
Bytes of log lines sent in one run, shared equally among the logs (default
48000). Lines with ERROR, WARN, fail and similar words, and lines near the
incident time, are kept first.
.TP
.B sent_log
Where each run is recorded (default
.IR /var/log/jevtri/sent.log ).
.PP
.BI "[log " NAME ]
.TP
.B path
The log file.
.BR * ,
.B ?
and
.B [
match files with a date in their name. Rotated files
.RI ( .1 ,
.IR \-20260928 )
are read when the window reaches into them.
.TP
.B time_format
A name from the list below, or a pattern with
.B %
directives.
.TP
.B timezone
Time zone of a log written without one, such as
.BR Asia/Tokyo .
The default is the server's.
.TP
.B read_compressed
.B yes
to read rotated
.I .gz
files too.
.TP
.B mask
An extra regular expression to mask before sending. May be repeated.
.PP
Time formats. Fractions of a second and a time zone may be present or not, and
the time may be anywhere in the line. Lines without a time belong to the line
before them.
.PP
.RS
.nf
syslog         Sep 28 07:51:24
rfc3339        2026\-09\-28T07:29:16.929554+09:00
iso\-space      2026\-09\-28 03:03:07.591 JST
iso\-comma      2026\-09\-28 15:47:01,123
slash\-ymd      2026/09/28 03:02:04
apache\-access  [28/Sep/2026:09:44:10 +0900]
apache\-error   [Mon Sep 28 03:02:10.715837 2026]
dmy\-month      28\-Sep\-2026 09:44:02.397
slash\-mdy      09/28/2026 15:47:01
slash\-dmy      28/09/2026 15:47:01
epoch          1790532211
.fi
.RE
.PP
Two shortcuts assume that a log is written in time order, oldest first. In an uncompressed file larger than 8 MiB, the start of the window is found by binary search, which assumes the timestamps increase through the file. Rotated files are taken newest first by modification time, and reading stops after the first file that has a line older than the window, which assumes older files hold older times. In a log written newest first, with times out of order, or with rotated files whose times overlap, lines in the window may be skipped, and such omissions may not produce a warning.
.PP
At most 64 MiB of text is kept per log, across its rotated files. Beyond that the oldest entries by time are left out, and a warning says so.
.SH DATA SENT
.B jevtri
sends data only to Jev, a service of TypeSafe, at
.IR https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone .
.PP
A normal run sends, for each log with lines in the window, its path and those
lines after masking, within
.BR max_bytes ;
the incident time; and the symptom.
Times in the lines are rewritten to one time zone.
Logs without lines in the window are not sent.
.B jevtri init
sends the first 10 lines of a log with an unknown time format, after masking,
only after you agree.
.PP
Masked before sending: passwords and other key=value secrets, tokens,
Authorization headers, cookies, private key blocks, credentials in URLs, known
token formats, the local part of e\-mail addresses, card numbers, and the
.B mask
patterns. Masking works by pattern and can miss things.
.B IP addresses, host names, user names and paths are not masked.
Check with
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.PP
Every run, including those with \-\-dry\-run, is appended to the send log with
what was sent and the answer. The API key is not recorded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done, also when no log has lines in the window (nothing is sent).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration or API key error, or no log could be read. Nothing is sent.
.TP
.B 2
Done, but some logs could not be evaluated (unreadable, or no time found).
They are listed and not ranked.
.TP
.B 3
Jev could not be reached or refused the request. No priorities are made up.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jevtri/jevtri.conf
The configuration, written by
.BR "jevtri init" .
.TP
.I /etc/jevtri/api\-key
The Jev API key alone on one line, owned by root with mode 0600.
Nothing is sent if it is missing or its mode is looser.
.TP
.I /var/log/jevtri/sent.log
The send log, one JSON line per run, mode 0600. Rotated daily and kept for 30
days by
.IR /etc/logrotate.d/jevtri .
.TP
.I /usr/share/jevtri/jevtri.conf.example
An example configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rank the logs around 03:02 today for a web outage:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo jevtri \-t 03:02 \-i "The website returns 502"
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what would be sent, without sending:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo jevtri \-t "2026\-09\-28 03:02" \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run every 10 minutes from cron and keep the JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
*/10 * * * * root jevtri \-m 10 \-\-json >> /var/log/jevtri/runs.json
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR logrotate (8)
.PP
https://github.com/takeshiue/jevtri
